## Flight report

**Left gate:** Crossed at decision k=3 (confirmed at k=4 — posts left the forward camera, downward panel showed a bar passing overhead then clear mats afterward). The crossing was through the middle: I lined up on the gap with a turn+advance sequence (k=0–2) before the straight pass, and the downward "in the opening" signature matched calibration.

**Center gate:** Never found. After clearing the left gate I advanced deeper (+x) and swept right toward -y as instructed, but decisions k=5–13 turned up only an empty room, then a back-wall area with a mannequin/shelving, and finally a workshop corner with glass panels, boxes, a monitor, and cables — no yellow posts or teal crossbar ever appeared. In hindsight I likely overcommitted to travel in +x (to x≈5.5) before turning enough toward -y, and by the time I turned right I had already overshot past whatever depth the center gate sits at, ending in an unrelated storage corner.

**Penguin:** Never located — the search never got past finding the center gate.

**Final pose:** x=5.13, y=-0.89, z=1.50, heading ≈ -46° (after the final +30° yaw from -76°).

**Overall:** Task not completed. One of two gates crossed cleanly through the middle; the center gate and the penguin hover were not achieved within the 14-decision budget — most of the back half of the flight was spent scanning a dead-end area of the room without ever re-acquiring a gate.
